Let $C$ divides $A B$ in the ratio $m: 1$. Then
$\mathbf{c}=\frac{m \mathbf{b}+\mathbf{a}}{m+1}\begin{array}{lr}\Rightarrow & m \mathbf{c}+\mathbf{c}=m \mathbf{b}+\mathbf{a} \\ \Rightarrow & \mathbf{a}+m \mathbf{b}-m \mathbf{c}-\mathbf{c}=\mathbf{0} \\ \Rightarrow & \mathbf{a}+m \mathbf{b}+(-m-1) \mathbf{c}=\mathbf{0}...(i)\end{array}
Given,
$\begin{array}{ll}
\text { Given, } & 3 a+4 b-7 c=0 \\
\Rightarrow & a+\frac{4}{3} b-\frac{7}{3} c=0...(ii)
\end{array}
On comparing Eqs. (i) and (ii), we get
$m=\frac{4}{3}\therefore$ Required ratio is $4: 3$

