Since, it passes through the points $(2,3,1)$ and $(4,-5,3)$.
$\begin{array}{lr}\therefore & 3 b+c+d=0 \\ \text { and } & -5 b+3 c+d=0\end{array}
$\begin{array}{ll}\Rightarrow & \frac{b}{1-3}=\frac{c}{-8}=\frac{d}{14} \\ \Rightarrow & \frac{b}{-2}=\frac{c}{-8}=\frac{d}{14}\end{array}
